---
# GitHub Actions workflows are the only YAML this repo has, and yamllint's
# "default" preset was written for YAML in general, not that dialect
# specifically -- two of its defaults fire on things GitHub Actions requires,
# not on anything wrong:
#
#   - `on:` is a literal top-level key every workflow needs. YAML 1.1 reads
#     the bareword `on` as the boolean true, which is the exact footgun that
#     made an earlier workflow need a comment explaining it -- but it is a MAP
#     KEY here, not a value, and GitHub's own parser treats it as the literal
#     string "on" regardless. `check-keys: false` stops the truthy check from
#     re-litigating a key spelling GitHub Actions itself mandates; `on` stays
#     in `allowed-values` so a stray bareword truthy VALUE (`foo: yes`) is
#     still caught.
#   - `document-start` wants a leading `---`. Vanishingly few real-world GitHub
#     Actions workflows carry one, GitHub's own docs and starter templates
#     never do, and requiring it here would be a repo-specific convention
#     imposed on a file format that doesn't use it anywhere else.
extends: default

rules:
  document-start: disable
  truthy:
    allowed-values: ["true", "false", "on"]
    check-keys: false
  # A pytest node id quoted in full in ci.yml can run long, precisely on
  # purpose. 100 gives that room
  # (80) enough to stop catching a line that has actually grown too long.
  line-length:
    max: 100
